{
  "id": "jet_propulsion",
  "title": "Jet Propulsion",
  "description": "Calculate jet propulsion velocity, flow volume, and thrust force using fluid dynamics equations. Applicable to incompressible flows such as liquids (water) but not gases (air).",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Jet Propulsion Calculator\n\n### Key Equations\n\n**Jet Velocity:** v₂ = √(2(p₁ - p₂)/ρ)\n\n**Volume Flow:** q = A × v₂\n\n**Propulsive Force (stationary jet):** F = 2A(p₁ - p₂)\n\n### Inputs"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "p1",
          "label": "Pressure Before Jet (p₁)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "defaultValue": 400000
        },
        {
          "id": "p2",
          "label": "Ambient Pressure After Jet (p₂)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "defaultValue": 100000
        },
        {
          "id": "rho",
          "label": "Fluid Density (ρ)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "kg/m³",
          "defaultValue": 1000
        },
        {
          "id": "area",
          "label": "Orifice Area (A)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m²",
          "defaultValue": 0.000177
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "velocity",
          "label": "Jet Velocity (v₂)",
          "formula": "Math.sqrt(2 * (inputs.p1 - inputs.p2) / inputs.rho)",
          "unit": "m/s",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "flow",
          "label": "Volume Flow (q)",
          "formula": "inputs.area * Math.sqrt(2 * (inputs.p1 - inputs.p2) / inputs.rho)",
          "unit": "m³/s",
          "format": "scientific"
        },
        {
          "id": "thrust",
          "label": "Propulsive Force (F)",
          "formula": "2 * inputs.area * (inputs.p1 - inputs.p2)",
          "unit": "N",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Parameter",
        "Symbol",
        "Value",
        "Unit",
        "Description"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Pressure Before Jet",
          "p₁",
          "Input",
          "Pa",
          "Absolute pressure upstream of the jet outlet"
        ],
        [
          "Ambient Pressure",
          "p₂",
          "Input",
          "Pa",
          "Atmospheric pressure after the jet"
        ],
        [
          "Fluid Density",
          "ρ",
          "Input",
          "kg/m³",
          "Density of incompressible fluid (e.g., water)"
        ],
        [
          "Orifice Area",
          "A",
          "Input",
          "m²",
          "Cross-sectional area of jet outlet"
        ],
        [
          "Jet Velocity",
          "v₂",
          "Calculated",
          "m/s",
          "Exit velocity from the jet"
        ],
        [
          "Volume Flow Rate",
          "q",
          "Calculated",
          "m³/s",
          "Volume of fluid flowing per unit time"
        ],
        [
          "Propulsive Force",
          "F",
          "Calculated",
          "N",
          "Thrust force generated by stationary jet"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "### Notes\n\n- **Valid for incompressible flows only** (liquids like water)\n- For a stationary jet: v₁ = 0\n- Equations assume constant fluid density\n- Not applicable for compressible flows (gases like air)\n\n### Example\n\nFor a garden hose with 15 mm diameter:\n- Orifice Area: A = π(0.0075)² = 1.77 × 10⁻⁴ m²\n- Pressure before: p₁ = 4 × 10⁵ Pa\n- Atmospheric pressure: p₂ = 1 × 10⁵ Pa\n- Propulsive Force: F = 2 × 1.77 × 10⁻⁴ × (4 × 10⁵ - 1 × 10⁵) = **106 N**"
    }
  ]
}